/**
 * @page external_parser Console-parser
 * @ingroup public_api
 * 
 * @section intro_parser Введение
 * 
 * **Console-parser** - This is an external module for parsing command-line arguments, integrated into UFO Console. 
 * It is located in the subdirectory `impl/Console-parser/`.
 *
 * https://github.com/onen-touw/Console-parser
 * 
 * @section features_parser Сapability
 * 
 * - Support for strict and non-strict modes
 * - Automatic type conversion (int, float, string, vector)
 * - Multiple aliases for options (например, `-v,--verbose`)
 * - Support for comma-separated arrays (`--numbers=1,2,3,4`)
 * - Support for large strings (double quotes) (`--message="Hello World"`)
 * - Автоматическое распознавание имени программы (первое слово)
 * 
 * @section usage_parser Usage in UFO Console
 * 
 * In UFO Console, the parser automatically parses each input line.
 * It is accessed via the @ref ufo::u_console_msg_block_t::get_opt_list():
 * 
 * @code{.cpp}
 * console.mk_blank("example", "Example command", [](const ufo::u_console_msg_block_t& bl) {
 *     const auto& parser = bl.get_opt_list();
 *     
 *     // Getting value
 *     int value = 0;
 *     if (parser.bind(&value, "-v,--value")) {
 *         bl << "Value: " << value << "\n";
 *     }
 *     
 *     // Checking for a flag
 *     if (parser.find("--verbose")) {
 *         bl << "Verbose mode enabled\n";
 *     }
 *     
 *     // Getting array
 *     std::vector<int> numbers;
 *     if (parser.bind(&numbers, "-n,--numbers")) {
 *         for (auto n : numbers) {
 *             bl << n << " ";
 *         }
 *         bl << "\n";
 *     }
 * });
 * @endcode
 * 
 * @section examples_parser Parsing examples
 * 
 * @subsection example_simple Arguments
 * 
 * Input string: `set --temp=25.5 --mode=fast`
 * 
 * @code{.cpp}
 * float temp;
 * std::string mode;
 * parser.bind(&temp, "--temp");
 * parser.bind(&mode, "--mode");
 * // temp = 25.5, mode = "fast"
 * @endcode
 * 
 * @subsection example_array Arrays
 * 
 * Input string: `average --values=10,20,30,40`
 * 
 * @code{.cpp}
 * std::vector<int> values;
 * parser.bind(&values, "--values");
 * // values = [10, 20, 30, 40]
 * @endcode
 * 
 * @subsection example_quoted Double quotes
 * 
 * Input string: `echo --message="Hello, World!"`
 * 
 * @code{.cpp}
 * std::string msg;
 * parser.bind(&msg, "--message");
 * // msg = Hello, World!
 * @endcode
 * 
 * @subsection example_aliases Aliases
 * 
 * Input string: `config -p=1234 --verbose`
 * 
 * @code{.cpp}
 * int port;
 * bool verbose;
 * parser.bind(&port, "-p,--port");     // найдет по -p
 * verbose = parser.find("--verbose");   // найдет --verbose
 * @endcode
 * 
 * @section methods_parser Basic methods
 * 
 * @copydoc Console_parser::parser::bind
 * @copydoc Console_parser::parser::find
 * @copydoc Console_parser::parser::get_prog_name
 * @copydoc Console_parser::parser::good
 * 
 * @section strict_mode Strict mode
 * 
 * The console is running in strict mode. (`parser(true)` in constructor of msg_block_t).
 * This means that if there is any error in the command syntax:
 * - The parser sets an error flag
 * - All bind() operations return false and bind nothing
 * - The user sees an error message
 * 
 * @section full_docs Full documentation
 * 
 * Full documentation for Console-parser is available in the file:
 * @link impl/Console-parser/parser.h parser.h @endlink
 * 
 * @see @ref ufo::u_console_msg_block_t::get_opt_list
 * @see Console_parser::parser
 */